UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53195950028330
DTSTART:20261111T230000Z
DTEND:20261112T003000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join the Gregg Museum of Art & Design for an evening that will 
 begin with an intimate artist talk by ariana Farquharson\, offering a behi
 nd-the-scenes look at the personal narratives and techniques that shaped t
 he exhibition\, You Are Here: Geolocating the Self through the Familiar in
  the Midst of the Unfamiliar. The exhibition will be on display in the art
  gallery at the African American Cultural Center from Oct. 28\, 2026\, to 
  Feb. 28\, 2027.
GEO:35.785108;-78.674529
LOCATION:Witherspoon Student Center\, African American Cultural Center (201
 )
SUMMARY:An Evening With ariana Farquharson
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/an-evening-with-ariana-farquh
 arson
CATEGORIES:Lectures and Talks
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC State Gregg Museum of Art & Design
DTSTAMP:20261114T061612Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54505683272884
DTSTART:20261201T233000Z
DTEND:20261202T013000Z
DESCRIPTION:As part of the Gregg Museum of Art & Design's ongoing explorati
 on of sanctuary\, community memory and collective care\, community histori
 an and cultural organizer Johnny Lee Chapman III will organize and facilit
 ate a series of intergenerational Story Circles. Centered on the voices of
  Black leaders and elders in Raleigh\, these gatherings are designed to co
 nnect deeply with young adults — the next generation of leaders.\n\nThro
 ugh facilitated dialogue and storytelling\, the Story Circles are inspired
  by the exhibitions at the Gregg Museum — Crafting Sanctuaries: Black Sp
 aces of the Great Depression South and Community Stories: Sustaining North
  Carolina’s Black Heritage — that will be on display during the Story 
 Circles. This series will explore how Black communities in Raleigh built n
 etworks of mutual support and sanctuary. These gatherings will create powe
 rful opportunities for Black elders and leaders to pass down lived histori
 es to NC State students and the broader community\, strengthening intergen
 erational dialogue and preserving vital community memory.\n\nJoin the muse
 um and Chapman for the Dec. 1 Story Circle\, featuring Carmen Wimberley Ca
 uthen\, a Raleigh native\, historian\, author and founder of Research and 
 Resource\, a historical research and community engagement firm.\n\nThis ev
 ent is free\, but registration is required. Space is limited to preserve t
 he intimacy of the circle.
GEO:35.784762;-78.661636
LOCATION:Gregg Museum of Art & Design
SUMMARY:Intergeneration Story Circle
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/intergeneration-story-circle
CATEGORIES:Lectures and Talks
CATEGORIES:Community Events
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
