X-SOURCE:NC State Gregg Museum of Art & Design
DTSTAMP:20261114T061612Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54381416854066
DTSTART:20270303T190000Z
DTEND:20270303T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:Please join the Data Science and AI Academy at the Gregg Museum
  of Art and Design for an exclusive AI Hot Topics event. The Gregg aims to
  create and hold space for the many perspectives surrounding artificial in
 telligence's growing presence in universities\, the arts and even in our e
 veryday lives. This hour-long conversation invites us to do more than take
  a side\; it asks us to listen first\, question and then challenge ourselv
 es to better understand where others are coming from. \n\nAs AI becomes in
 creasingly present in creative spaces\, questions about ethics\, authorshi
 p and what may be at stake for artistic expression continue to emerge. Joi
 n us for an open conversation exploring AI's place in the arts and the pos
 sibilities and concerns that have come with it.\n\nArtists\, students\, fa
 culty and community members will unpack and share various presepctives of 
 who gets to define art and the very real ethical concerns surrounding AI
 ’s impact\, particularly in the arts and education.
GEO:35.784762;-78.661636
LOCATION:Gregg Museum of Art & Design
SUMMARY:Gregg Museum Edition: AI Hot Topics: Does AI Have a Place in the A(
 a)rts?
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/the-gregg-museum-edition-ai-h
 ot-topics-does-ai-have-a-place-in-the-aarts
CATEGORIES:Lectures and Talks
END:VEVENT
