DESCRIPTION:NC State LIVE and the Gregg Museum of Art & Design have partner
 ed to present Well-Being Concerts\, featuring a family with rich connectio
 ns to the university and the museum. The late architect Phil Freelon\, an 
 NC State College of Design alumnus\, led the team that designed the Gregg
 ’s new home\, which opened in 2017. Phil Freelon's widow and son\, Nnenn
 a and Pierce Freelon\, are a Grammy-nominated mother-son musical duo known
  for their collaborative children’s album\, AnceStars. Nnenna Freelon is
  an acclaimed composer\, podcaster\, author and advocate for arts educatio
 n. In addition to his music career\, Pierce Freelon is a picture book auth
 or\, podcaster and ice cream maker. The duo will perform at the Gregg insi
 de the gallery featuring the exhibition Grounded by artist-in-residence Ma
 ya Freelon\, Phil and Nnenna Freelon’s daughter. Shaped by Maya Freelon
 ’s personal and collective memory\, ancestry and humanity\, Grounded tra
 nsforms the Gregg into a retrospective on well-being\, connection and disc
 overy. \n\nThis concert was created in partnership with Carnegie Hall’s 
 Weill Music Institute. Carnegie Hall’s Well-Being Concerts combine world
 -class musical performances with elements of self-care and mindfulness\, a
 nimated by evidence that music helps people heal and thrive.
GEO:35.784762;-78.661636
LOCATION:Gregg Museum of Art & Design\, Galleries and Main Lobby
SUMMARY:NC State LIVE Well-Being Concerts With Nnenna and Pierce Freelon
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/nc-state-live-well-being-conc
 erts-with-nnenna-and-pierce-freelon
